ry kept, caught at entry k). Assert error mentions entry k. - truncate after entry m → final root mismatch (C5-final) OR missing-seq detection if head_seq receipt known: check count vs receipt. seq → C2/count mismatch. - duplicate entry k (insert copy) → seq ! - swap payloads of entries j,k (same len) → prev_root still fine? prev_root fields unchanged; leaf hashes differ → final root mismatch; with per-entry receipts, pinpointed at j. - mutate ts of entry 0 to be > ts of 1 → C3. - corrupt magic → C1. - oversize plen field edit without payload → plen ! All mutations applied to the extracted stream, re-fed to verifier with original receipts → must raise with expected label. This demonstrates tamper-evidence concretely. Also test CAS: two writers race on same ref; second update-ref fails nonzero → rejected append (state unchanged). Maybe include briefly. I must ensure code is actually correct. Let me write the MMR functions carefully and mentally test on small sizes. peaks list: elements (height:int, hash:bytes). Invariant after each append: heights strictly decreasing. append_leaf(peaks, leaf_hash): node = (0, leaf_hash) while peaks and peaks[-1][0] == node[0]: node = (l[0]+1, sha256(b"\x01" + l[1] + node[1]). - add L0: peaks=[(0,L0)] - add L1: node=(0,L1); top height 0 ==0 → pop L0, node=(1,H(L0||L1)); peaks empty → push → [(1,H01)] - add L2: [(1,H01),(0,L2)] - add L3: node=(0,L3); pop L2 → node=(1,H(L2||L3)); top (1,H01) equal → pop → node=(2,H(H01||H23)); push → [(2,. Good: heights strictly decreasing ✓. it = reversed(peaks)  # smallest/newest first for _,h in it: acc = h if acc is None else sha256(b"\x01"+h+acc). Trace 3 leaves: peaks=[(1,A),(0,C)]. reversed: C → acc=C; then A: acc=H(A||C). Root=H(A||C) with older-left ✓ consistent with merge orientation (left operand = earlier peak). Empty log: bag([]) → define None → return EMPTY_ROOT explicitly. Verify loop maintains running head_root = bag(peaks_so_far) after each append; compare with receipts[i]. root when pe